  "catalogueCode": "SPW-B/052-b",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A desiccated world whose seas went twice: once when the primary brightened, and again when the white dwarf&#39;s progenitor shed its envelope and stripped away what was left. What remains is a set of closed basins floored in salt to a depth of three hundred metres, ringed by dunes that are still moving, with fresh water only in aquifers that have to be reached. The population is small, dispersed, and organised entirely around where the water is. It is the only inhabited world in the Seventh Shell still open to contact.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    },
    {
      "value": "<p>Izsušen svet z zaprtimi solnimi kotanjami; vsa naselja so vezana na vodonosnike.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "sl-SI"] }]
    }
  ],
